<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3ba8fe46-6a06-56ab-aff6-9fa9ef988a37" activityNameId="5ba220cc-5a3d-5f05-89ed-96a09a392da7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, nuclear, at power plant pressure water reactor</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, nuclear, at power plant pressure water reactor
The dataset has been developed on the basis of the operation of the FR PRW (without MOX and without reprocessing of spent fuel) with average burnup of 42.5 MWd/kg heavy metal assumed representative for the lifetime of the modeled plant. The average burnup corresponds to an average enrichment of 3.8% U235 for fresh uranium fuel elements. The utilisation factor for the infrastructure is the inverse of the total net electricity delivered in 40 years lifetime, calculated assuming an average Load Factor = 80% (1998-2003 it spanned 70-88%). Same thermal efficiency as for PWR CH. Material requirements have been extrapolated from the Swiss PWR by the ratio of the capacity factors. The transport requirements are calculated either using ecoinvent standard distances for Europe (e.g. for chemicals) or given average distances by train from Chinese 2004 statistics or own assumptions. Radioactive emission species to air and water are those calculated for UCTE PWRs around year 2000. The radioactive waste streams are modeled as such: all spent fuel to conditioning;
UUID: 45c5821e-cf95-3d4d-a8f1-525a18bfe93d
The module includes fuel elements, chemicals, and diesel requirements as well as the relevant transport requirements. Water use (fresh from sea and decarbonized) for cooling is included. Considered radioactive waste streams are: spent fuel to conditioning (no reprocessing); operational low active waste for conditioning in the intermediate repository; and, contaminated waste from dismantling. Non-radioactive wastes are accounted for.
Location: Swiss data of one specific plant for requirements and UCTE PWRs for radioactive emissions.
Technology: Standard technology for commercial operation.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature and statistics of radioactive emissions. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_45c5821e-cf95-3d4d-a8f1-525a18bfe93d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
